<h2 id="rules">The rules</h2>
<table class="tbl">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Rule</th>
      <th>Scope</th>
      <th>Importance</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>
        <strong>Await where the data is used</strong> - the blocking scope of a request is
        exactly the subtree behind the await.
      </td>
      <td><Chip k="react" /></td>
      <td><Chip k="critical" /></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>
        Independent requests run <strong>in parallel</strong> - sibling self-fetching
        components, or <code>Promise.all</code> within one component. Never serialized
        awaits for unrelated data.
      </td>
      <td><Chip k="react" /></td>
      <td><Chip k="critical" /></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>
        Dependent chains are <strong>confined to the smallest region</strong> that needs
        their result.
      </td>
      <td><Chip k="react" /></td>
      <td><Chip k="very" /></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>
        Regions deserving route-level independence become
        <strong>parallel-route slots</strong> - own loading, own error, own stream.
      </td>
      <td><Chip k="next" /></td>
      <td><Chip k="very" /></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>
        Every slot defines <strong><code>default.tsx</code></strong> - unmatched
        navigation must not 404 the route.
      </td>
      <td><Chip k="next" /></td>
      <td><Chip k="critical" /></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>
        No client-side dependent query chains -
        <strong>resolve dependencies on the server</strong>, or collapse them into one
        key.
      </td>
      <td><Chip k="react" /></td>
      <td><Chip k="critical" /></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

